      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if the checks implemented below / supported by SkStream API are sufficient to check if **all** the input data is available.  If (for example) only the first 1024 bytes (of a **bigger** input) are available, then IIUC `SkStream::hasLength` will return `true` (e.g. see [`blink::SegmentStream::hasLength`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/image-decoders/skia/segment_stream.cc;l\u003d115-117;drc\u003d30341531e02ec37f096b896932f227b6bd51d635)) and `SkStream::getLength` will return 1024 (e.g. see [`blink::SegmentStream::getLength`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/image-decoders/skia/segment_stream.cc;l\u003d119-125;drc\u003d30341531e02ec37f096b896932f227b6bd51d635)), eventually returning `isAtEnd` (e.g. see [Blink implementation here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/image-decoders/skia/segment_stream.cc;l\u003d87-89;drc\u003d30341531e02ec37f096b896932f227b6bd51d635)).\n\nI am not sure what can be done about this - I hope that @fmalita can chime in with suggestions.  I wonder if a new API (`virtual std::optional\u003cbool\u003e SkStream::hasAllData()`) could potentially be added to Skia (`nullopt` \u003d\u003e don\u0027t know or unimplemented;  false \u003d don\u0027t have all the data, true \u003d have all the data).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "d4d3d48d3873bd086a207a811f221186d80e61da",
